{"kind":"assert","text":"Clarifying condition 1 of this request, with hugh's approval on 2026-10-16. \"The preflights of state, batch, ratify and supersede\" means their event-reference resolution, which opens through the shared session opener. It does not mean the chain preflight or admission. Those fold the local verified log before signing by design: admission is judged on the local verified log, as docs/reference/architecture.md layer 7 states. The independent review of head 89c4603b measured that local preflight fold at about 54 s per command on a frozen artroom copy at depth 43,744. That cost is not owed under this request; a separate request tracks it."}